In the provided code, the comment "// @@@ size of array is always greater than or equal to 0" is what we need to convert into an assert statement. I have used the `OLD(_size)` syntax to refer to the old value of `_size` before it is changed inside the `Count` getter. The `Count` getter returns the value of `_size`, so `OLD(_size)` gives the value `_size` had just before the `Count` was accessed. The assertion checks that this old value is always less than or equal to the current value of `Count`, which should always be true since `_size` is only ever increased. The current value of `Count` is always less than or equal to the current `_items.Length`, which is the capacity, so the assertion also checks that the current value of `Count` is less than or equal to the capacity.
--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) >= 0);
</code>
--------------------